    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14">
        <head>Cn 1018 14</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#kennedy" n="14" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="76" ed="#kennedy"/>And ealle godes gerihta friðige man georne. ealswa hit þearf is. 7 freolsa 7 fæstena healde man rihtlice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="218" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ealle Godes gerihta friðige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is, and freolsa and fæstena healde man rihtlice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#kennedy" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="76" ed="#kennedy"/>And all ecclesiastical dues shall be protected zealously, as there is need to do, and festivals and fasts duly observed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="219" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And all God’s dues are to be given willingly, just as is required, and feasts and fasts are to be properly observed.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:ICn_14">I Cn 14–14.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 14-14:1: Cn 1018 14-14:1 (Hom N L) VI Atr 21:1-22</quote></note>
      </div>
    </body>
